{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For a U.S. ’40 Act ETF launch, core arrangements include:\n\n- **Governance:** Registered fund/trust, board with required independent representation, officers, chief compliance officer, compliance policies, investment adviser and approved advisory agreements. An existing series trust can supply much of this framework.\n- **Fund services:** Custody, administration, fund accounting/NAV calculation, transfer agency, principal underwriting/distribution, legal counsel and an independent registered public accounting firm.\n- **Market infrastructure:** Exchange listing; DTC eligibility and applicable NSCC creation/redemption processing; authorized-participant agreements; basket publication and processing; required website disclosures; and exchange-required market-maker arrangements. APs create/redeem shares; market makers quote and trade them—one firm may perform both.\n- **Conditional arrangements:** Index methodology, calculation and licensing for index strategies; lending authorization, borrower/collateral administration and typically a lending agent only if operating a securities-lending program; subadvisers or derivatives documentation where applicable.\n\n**Worth knowing:** These are functions, not separate-firm requirements. Providers commonly bundle services, subject to independence, conflict and oversight requirements."}}
